GOAD range templates
=====================

The range templates in this directory (goad.json, goad-light.json,
goad-mini.json, goad-wazuh.json, nha.json, sccm.json, dracarys.json, and
minilab.json) are derived from GOAD (Game of Active Directory) and its family of
vulnerable Active Directory labs by Orange Cyberdefense:

    https://github.com/Orange-Cyberdefense/GOAD

GOAD is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. These templates
reproduce GOAD's lab content (its domains, hosts, users, groups, and planted
attack paths) as redStackPRO range documents, and are therefore a derivative
work of GOAD. They are distributed under the same license, GPLv3, a copy of
which sits alongside this notice in LICENSE.

This applies only to the files in this directory. The rest of redStackPRO,
including the code that reads and writes the GOAD config format, is the project's
own work under the MIT license (see the repository LICENSE). goad-wazuh.json adds
the Wazuh and ws01 extensions on top of GOAD-Light; those additions are the
project's, but the file as a whole remains a GOAD derivative and stays GPLv3.

goad-wazuh.json is redStackPRO's composition on top of GOAD-Light; goad.json,
goad-light.json, goad-mini.json, nha.json (Ninja Hacker Academy), sccm.json,
dracarys.json, and minilab.json follow the upstream GOAD, GOAD-Light, GOAD-Mini,
NHA, SCCM, DRACARYS, and MINI labs respectively.
